WEBVTT

00:07.320 --> 00:09.150
<i>Video games are wonderful.</i>

00:09.710 --> 00:11.370
<i>I might be a 38-year-old man,</i>

00:11.370 --> 00:13.500
<i>but when I'm in a game, I'm young again.</i>

00:13.820 --> 00:18.970
<i>And I can do things that
 I could never do in real life.</i>

00:18.970 --> 00:22.640
<i>Okay, time to start by making my character.</i>

00:22.980 --> 00:25.430
<i>I'll name him "Earth," I guess.</i>

00:25.430 --> 00:26.660
<i>Since Daichi's my real name.</i>

00:26.980 --> 00:29.220
<i>And I'll make him look... young.</i>

00:29.700 --> 00:32.050
<i>He can be the same height as me...</i>

00:32.480 --> 00:35.080
<i>And he definitely needs 
black hair and black eyes.</i>

00:35.080 --> 00:37.340
<i>There. That should do it.</i>

00:38.170 --> 00:44.240
<i>He doesn't exactly stand out, but I'm not 
the type to be the main character myself.</i>

00:45.120 --> 00:47.190
<i>I'm a salaryman in the real world.</i>

00:47.190 --> 00:50.440
<i>I can only play two or three hours a day.</i>

00:50.440 --> 00:53.360
<i>So I might cause trouble for other 
players if I tried to play with them.</i>

00:53.360 --> 00:56.290
<i>I'll be going solo 
most of the time, I bet.</i>

00:56.690 --> 01:00.380
<i>Now to pick my skills. I can pick mostly 
things that were underpowered...</i>

01:00.380 --> 01:02.890
<i>or, let's be honest, trash, during the beta.</i>

01:02.410 --> 01:10.130
Archery

01:02.910 --> 01:10.130
Kick

01:03.410 --> 01:10.130
Long-Distance
Vision

01:03.910 --> 01:10.130
Wind Magic

01:04.770 --> 01:08.300
<i>Then the hardcore crowd will leave me alone,</i>

01:05.660 --> 01:10.130
Production Fingertips

01:06.170 --> 01:10.130
Cooking

01:06.670 --> 01:10.130
Woodworking

01:07.670 --> 01:10.130
Medicine

01:08.040 --> 01:10.130
Sneak

01:08.300 --> 01:10.110
<i>and I play the game at my own pace.</i>

01:08.670 --> 01:10.130
Improved
Physical Abilities

01:10.820 --> 01:13.260
<i>Out of my ten skills, six are underpowered.</i>

01:13.260 --> 01:15.550
<i>Bows are supposed to have 
really bad accuracy.</i>

01:16.080 --> 01:23.180
<i>And potions are available cheap from NPCs, 
so medicine's pretty worthless.</i>

01:23.930 --> 01:26.510
<i>Kick has no special attacks.</i>

01:26.510 --> 01:28.660
<i>You can't beat an enemy in 
one hit just by kicking it.</i>

01:29.230 --> 01:33.010
<i>Wind Magic is worse than the 
other types for attacking.</i>

01:33.010 --> 01:37.230
<i>It doesn't work against Fire and 
it's useless against Earth.</i>

01:38.210 --> 01:40.640
<i>Sneak has a high MP cost.</i>

01:40.640 --> 01:44.270
<i>If you move, it's easy to find you, so it's 
not good for trying to run away from monsters.</i>

01:44.870 --> 01:49.470
<i>Improved Physical Abilities supposedly gives a 
bonus to running, using a weapon, or crafting.</i>

01:49.470 --> 01:53.660
<i>But it's a small bonus, 
so if you want to be strong,</i>

01:53.660 --> 01:57.690
<i>you should pick something more specialized.</i>

01:58.150 --> 02:01.750
<i>But by picking skills that are underpowered,</i>

01:59.050 --> 02:07.230
<b>Improved Physical Abilities

 Long-Distance Vision
 Sneak
 Bow
 Wind Magic
 Production Fingertips
 Cooking
 Medicine
 Woodworking
 Kick</b>

02:01.750 --> 02:03.760
<i>other people won't want to play with me.</i>

02:03.760 --> 02:06.090
<i>So I can relax and play my way.</i>

02:06.090 --> 02:08.440
That's it for making my character!

02:08.440 --> 02:10.530
Time for my first log-in!

02:15.860 --> 02:24.120
<b>A Playthrough of a Certain DUDE's
VRMMO LIFE</b>

03:41.450 --> 03:45.450
<b>Episode 1</b>

03:41.450 --> 03:45.450
<b>Earth Logs In</b>

03:43.540 --> 03:46.730
<i>The concept of One More Free Life Online is,
 like the name says,</i>

03:46.730 --> 03:50.610
<i>that you can enjoy another life here.</i>

03:51.520 --> 03:54.690
<i>There's no big "Beat the Final Boss" quest,</i>

03:54.690 --> 03:57.590
<i>so you're free to spend all 
your time fighting monsters,</i>

03:58.160 --> 04:02.280
<i>or being a craftsperson who 
specializes on making items.</i>

04:02.680 --> 04:07.070
<i>Or you can just hang out 
and talk to other players.</i>

04:07.070 --> 04:10.980
<i>You can play the game however you want.</i>

04:12.160 --> 04:15.880
It's the first day, so the place is packed.

04:15.880 --> 04:19.010
You're a new player, right? 
How about some equipment?

04:19.010 --> 04:20.370
We've got the good stuff!

04:28.120 --> 04:30.430
<i>I guess there aren't any archers, huh?</i>

04:31.980 --> 04:34.120
You there, loser.

04:34.450 --> 04:36.550
The one with the bow.

04:36.550 --> 04:39.610
This is an unlucky way 
to start my first day...

04:39.610 --> 04:40.970
You mean me?

04:40.970 --> 04:42.840
Don't you know that bows are useless?

04:43.280 --> 04:46.210
I guess some people are just weird!

04:46.850 --> 04:48.560
And you've got the face of a loser.

04:48.560 --> 04:51.000
You're such a dork!

04:51.560 --> 04:52.670
Let's go!

04:54.060 --> 04:56.570
Hah! Look at that loser lying in the road!

04:56.120 --> 04:58.000
Hey, is the new player okay?

04:57.490 --> 04:59.540
I guess they didn't like the bow...

04:58.890 --> 05:01.490
Glad I picked a sword!

05:01.840 --> 05:04.510
Hey, be careful, newbie!

05:03.050 --> 05:06.000
<i>I guess people really don't like archers.</i>

05:05.010 --> 05:06.830
Come back any time!

05:06.000 --> 05:08.320
<i>That's better for me, though.</i>

05:07.400 --> 05:08.910
Welcome!

05:12.200 --> 05:13.580
<b>Training Hall</b>

05:13.590 --> 05:15.550
Oh, look at 'em all working hard!

05:15.550 --> 05:16.750
Okay, I'll try, too!

05:19.670 --> 05:20.130
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:21.180 --> 05:23.550
<i>I can't even shoot the thing...</i>

05:23.970 --> 05:25.680
Guess I've gotta practice!

05:26.470 --> 05:26.930
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:26.880 --> 05:30.290
Take this, and this, and this, and this!

05:27.340 --> 05:27.800
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:28.090 --> 05:28.550
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:28.800 --> 05:29.260
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:28.970 --> 05:29.430
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:29.090 --> 05:29.550
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:29.300 --> 05:29.760
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:29.590 --> 05:30.050
<b>Whiff...</b>

05:30.690 --> 05:33.890
<i>It's even less accurate than I'd heard!</i>

05:34.350 --> 05:34.770
<b>Thock</b>

05:35.410 --> 05:39.290
<i>I fired 100 shots and made it to level 5.</i>

05:37.310 --> 05:39.980
<b>Archery</b>

05:40.750 --> 05:43.700
Veni Ventus Volare.

05:43.700 --> 05:45.340
Wind Needle!

05:45.490 --> 05:48.700
<b>Wind Magic</b>

05:45.940 --> 05:48.290
It's more accurate than archery.

05:48.990 --> 05:51.730
And my kick skill's gone way up, too...

05:52.990 --> 05:54.700
<b>Kick</b>

05:56.190 --> 05:59.760
<i>Okay, I've got the minimum skills 
I need to survive out there.</i>

05:59.760 --> 06:01.710
<i>Time to head out into the field!</i>

06:01.710 --> 06:03.120
I saw one over there! Get it!

06:03.120 --> 06:04.050
Out of the way!

06:04.050 --> 06:05.950
That's my prey!

06:06.290 --> 06:07.990
Looks like a mess.

06:07.990 --> 06:09.690
I guess I won't be doing any combat today.

06:09.690 --> 06:12.330
I'll focus on gathering herbs.

06:15.220 --> 06:21.230
<b>Long-Distance Vision</b>

06:25.320 --> 06:28.540
<i>So you don't know what it is 
after you pick it up, huh?</i>

06:28.870 --> 06:30.900
<i>I guess I'll go back and appraise it.</i>

06:31.460 --> 06:33.220
I lost another one?

06:34.130 --> 06:39.320
<i>At first, I kept messing up and losing 
my herbs before I could identify them.</i>

06:39.660 --> 06:42.970
<i>But I'm starting to figure it out.</i>

06:42.970 --> 06:44.460
<i>And the reason for that is...</i>

06:44.590 --> 06:47.590
<b>Medicine</b>

06:44.590 --> 06:47.590
<b>Medicinal Herb x1</b>

06:44.590 --> 06:47.590
Found In: First
Explanation: Used for potions.
Effect: Restores 3% HP
Type: Medicine Item
Rarity: Common

06:45.480 --> 06:47.430
<i>My medicine level is going up,</i>

06:47.430 --> 06:51.390
<i>and I've been able to figure out 
which category an herb is in.</i>

06:47.590 --> 06:50.050
<b>Medicine</b>

06:47.590 --> 06:50.050
<b>Grass x2</b>

06:47.590 --> 06:50.050
Found In: First
Explanation: Just some
ordinary grass.
Effect: None
Type: Medicine Item
Rarity: Common

06:50.050 --> 06:51.390
<b>Medicine</b>

06:50.050 --> 06:51.390
<b>Antidote Herb x1</b>

06:50.050 --> 06:51.390
Found In: First
Explanation: Useless on its own.
Can be used as an antidote ingredient.
Effect: None
Type: Medicine Item Rarity: Common

06:51.770 --> 06:56.880
<i>The problem is that I found two of </i>these!<i></i>

06:58.640 --> 07:02.190
[Suffocation Herb] Whoever eats this will instantly stop breathing and die.
Do not eat under any circumstances!

07:02.380 --> 07:05.700
What was I supposed to do if I didn't 
use appraise on these first?

07:05.700 --> 07:09.110
What were the devs thinking, 
putting this in the first area?

07:10.640 --> 07:16.790
<i>I went to a potion store and used my starting 
cash to buy a beginner's medicine crafting set.</i>

07:16.790 --> 07:19.400
<i>The method to make healing potions...</i>

07:20.000 --> 07:21.190
<i>It's just what I thought.</i>

07:21.190 --> 07:25.970
<i>You grind up the herb, soak it in
 clean water, heat it, and you're done.</i>

07:27.300 --> 07:31.220
<b>[Common Healing Potion]
 The most basic of all healing items.</b>

07:31.540 --> 07:35.880
<i>In this game, once you've made 
an item, you can batch craft it.</i>

07:32.010 --> 07:39.480
<b>Crafting</b>

07:35.010 --> 07:39.480
<b>Batch Crafting</b>

07:35.880 --> 07:38.920
<i>The items aren't as high-quality, 
but it's much easier.</i>

07:40.470 --> 07:44.390
Guess I'll make some potions 
and antidotes for tomorrow!

07:45.190 --> 07:49.030
<b>[Common Anti-Poison Potion]
The weakest antidote potion.</b>

07:51.280 --> 07:57.950
<b>Medicine</b>

07:51.390 --> 07:54.270
<i>My medicine skill is at level 7!</i>

07:54.270 --> 07:57.950
<i>And my Production Fingertips 
skill went up a bit, as well!</i>

07:58.220 --> 08:02.860
<i>But you can get potions for 
really cheap from NPCs,</i>

08:02.860 --> 08:05.880
<i>so nobody's going to want these.</i>

08:07.540 --> 08:09.760
Now it's time to go hunting!

08:12.540 --> 08:15.340
It's finally emptied out!

08:15.750 --> 08:20.160
I won't have to argue with other players 
about who gets to fight a monster.

08:26.720 --> 08:30.730
<i>You can't fire quickly with a bow, 
so the first shot is really important.</i>

08:33.270 --> 08:34.930
It noticed me?

08:39.890 --> 08:41.030
I got it!

08:53.800 --> 08:55.220
<b>You got rabbithorn meat
and a rabbithorn pelt.</b>

08:55.460 --> 08:58.840
I'm less of an archer and 
more of a kicker, huh?

08:58.840 --> 09:00.780
Gwaaaahh!

09:03.140 --> 09:05.200
That was hilarious!

09:07.510 --> 09:08.350
What?

09:08.350 --> 09:10.000
"What," he says!

09:10.460 --> 09:12.380
You're laughing too much.

09:13.840 --> 09:15.310
But, Millie!

09:15.310 --> 09:18.190
So, what was so funny?

09:18.870 --> 09:20.080
Sorry, sorry!

09:20.080 --> 09:26.250
I've fought rabbithorns before, but I've 
never seen one make a noise like that!

09:26.250 --> 09:30.150
It was like, "Fwraaaaaagghhh!"

09:32.220 --> 09:34.500
Humor is justice!

09:34.780 --> 09:36.950
So you're a comedian or something?

09:36.950 --> 09:38.790
Sorry.

09:39.390 --> 09:41.770
You seem pretty cool.

09:42.210 --> 09:43.310
I'm Zwei.

09:43.310 --> 09:44.460
This is Millie.

09:45.360 --> 09:47.050
I can send a friend request, right?

09:47.050 --> 09:49.680
May I send one, too?

09:49.680 --> 09:51.410
Sure, but...

09:51.410 --> 09:53.030
Awesome!

09:53.030 --> 09:54.310
I've got a partner now!

09:54.710 --> 09:57.450
Time to aim for being a top comedic duo!

09:57.450 --> 09:58.950
I'm not your partner!

09:58.950 --> 10:00.830
That was perfect!

09:58.950 --> 10:03.450
<b>Friend {something}</b>

10:00.830 --> 10:03.010
Let's party up some time!

10:03.400 --> 10:05.150
See you around, okay?

10:05.150 --> 10:06.030
Sure.

10:10.110 --> 10:14.700
<i>It took way too long to take 
out a single monster...</i>

10:14.700 --> 10:16.750
<i>I need to get more experience.</i>

10:21.610 --> 10:24.760
<i>They notice me even when I try to 
hit them from their blind spots.</i>

10:25.080 --> 10:27.360
Veni Ventus Volare!

10:27.360 --> 10:29.070
Wind Needle!

10:28.190 --> 10:29.060
<b>Wind Needle</b>

10:32.280 --> 10:35.720
<i>Wind Needle's a wind spell, so it hits...</i>

10:35.720 --> 10:37.980
<i>But how do I stay hidden from them?</i>

10:39.490 --> 10:41.450
<b>Sneak</b>

10:39.950 --> 10:41.850
<i>My sneak skill?</i>

10:41.850 --> 10:43.900
<i>It's worth a try!</i>

10:48.710 --> 10:53.590
Critical Hit

10:48.710 --> 10:53.590
<b>Secret Attack "Pinpoint Hit" successful!</b>

10:54.420 --> 10:58.570
The bow never hits, and you 
can't use sneak to run away.

10:58.570 --> 11:02.040
But put them together, 
and they're really strong!

11:02.950 --> 11:06.310
I think I'm seeing what my next step is!

11:11.300 --> 11:14.270
The hardcore crowd will be 
up all night, I'm sure.

11:15.180 --> 11:17.950
But I've got work tomorrow.

11:18.370 --> 11:19.560
Time to go to bed.

11:29.050 --> 11:32.320
What's with this bread? 
It's pretty unimpressive.

11:32.320 --> 11:35.660
The stuff you buy from NPCs 
doesn't taste that good.

11:36.040 --> 11:39.580
If you can taste stuff in this game,

11:39.580 --> 11:42.470
I'd like to be able to eat 
something that tastes better.

11:47.050 --> 11:50.410
<i>I've got my seasonings and cooking set...</i>

11:50.410 --> 11:52.070
<i>Time to get to work!</i>

11:54.470 --> 11:58.890
<i>First, I'll start by just frying 
the meat to see how it tastes,</i>

11:58.890 --> 12:01.200
<i>then season it with salt and pepper.</i>

12:01.990 --> 12:04.480
<i>My very first rabbit steak!</i>

12:02.030 --> 12:04.910
<b>[Rabbit Steak]
A simply-prepared serving of rabbithorn meat.</b>

12:08.210 --> 12:10.660
It's tough! It's way too tough!

12:13.140 --> 12:15.560
So its score is 2, huh?

12:16.430 --> 12:20.380
<i>Now I'll try making cuts in 
it and preparing it properly.</i>

12:21.210 --> 12:24.570
<i>And I'll put some herbs in to 
get rid of the gamy taste.</i>

12:26.800 --> 12:28.680
<b>[Rabbit Herb Steak]
A serving of rabbithorn steak prepared with fragrant herbs.
Proper preparation has made the meat much more tender.</b>

12:32.530 --> 12:34.810
It's tender and delicious!

12:36.310 --> 12:38.560
It's got a score of 5, huh?

12:38.960 --> 12:42.100
I'd love to get it up another point or two.

12:39.070 --> 12:42.650
<b>Score: 5</b>

12:43.520 --> 12:45.940
<i>Scoring it was definitely the right idea.</i>

12:46.370 --> 12:49.040
<i>Now I'll try to parboil it a little before frying.</i>

12:55.770 --> 12:58.780
What's that tantalizing, 
herbaceous aroma I'm smelling?

12:58.780 --> 13:00.960
It's making me so hungry!

13:00.960 --> 13:04.250
Why would I smell meat in a place 
like this? It smells so good!

13:01.870 --> 13:03.480
I've never smelled anything like it!

13:02.980 --> 13:04.270
Where's it coming from?

13:05.630 --> 13:07.970
<b>[Parboiled Rabbit Steak With Herbs]
The meat of a rabbithorn, lovingly prepared by parboiling it before frying.
The parboiling liquid was flavored with herbs, as well.</b>

13:08.850 --> 13:11.450
I finally got a score of 7!

13:11.450 --> 13:13.490
I'm satisfied with this!

13:13.490 --> 13:15.030
Let me have some!

13:15.380 --> 13:19.860
You can't make something that smells 
this good and not give us any!

13:22.290 --> 13:24.440
O-Okay!

13:25.450 --> 13:28.070
A hundred gloh per steak!

13:28.070 --> 13:29.040
<i>How about that?</i>

13:29.040 --> 13:32.210
<i>That's about 20 times what 
it costs to buy bread from the NPCs!</i>

13:32.210 --> 13:32.970
I'll take it!

13:32.970 --> 13:35.250
I'll pay, just give it to me!

13:37.980 --> 13:38.870
Is it ready yet?

13:38.870 --> 13:40.230
Just a little more!

13:40.230 --> 13:41.930
Where's mine?

13:41.930 --> 13:43.380
Wait, I said!

13:43.460 --> 13:52.810
End of Line

13:43.840 --> 13:51.080
<i>And so I spent the evening in cooking hell, 
but I crafted enough to get to cooking level 20.</i>

13:46.600 --> 13:48.010
Why is everyone lined up?

13:48.010 --> 13:50.950
To try the delicious rabbit steak!

13:50.950 --> 13:52.790
Hold this and stand here, okay?

13:52.810 --> 13:55.480
<b>Cooking Promotion</b>

13:53.060 --> 13:55.210
<i>And I learned Cooking Promotion!</i>

13:55.490 --> 13:57.180
Here you go!

13:57.180 --> 14:00.380
<i>Thanks to that, I was able 
to cook at high speed,</i>

14:00.380 --> 14:03.400
<i>and finally escape that hell.</i>

14:05.660 --> 14:08.870
<i>And now I'm making a bow.</i>

14:08.870 --> 14:12.320
<i>There's no demand for bows so 
you have to make them yourself.</i>

14:12.630 --> 14:17.440
<i>I'm going to start by making the 
simplest bow out of just a piece of wood.</i>

14:18.210 --> 14:21.320
<i>I'll sand it down carefully and add 
something to make it less slippery.</i>

14:21.680 --> 14:25.060
<i>Make the grips and tie the string...</i>

14:26.880 --> 14:30.390
<b>[Beginner's Wooden Crafted Bow]
Probably too weak to use against monsters. 
Atk+4 Score: 3</b>

14:30.390 --> 14:33.550
<i>A score of three and an attack of four, huh?</i>

14:33.550 --> 14:36.100
<i>It's better than the basic 
beginner's bow, I guess.</i>

14:36.100 --> 14:37.760
<i>I guess I can try some other stuff.</i>

14:38.570 --> 14:40.390
<i>I can put together three pieces of wood,</i>

14:40.390 --> 14:44.100
<i>two made from a harder material 
and one that's more flexible...</i>

14:44.640 --> 14:49.070
<i>Then sand down the parts that face each 
other so they fit together and bend.</i>

14:50.030 --> 14:53.490
<b>[Prototype Compound Wood Bow]
A bow made by combining multiple types of wood together.
Atk +12 Score: 5</b>

14:53.480 --> 14:55.940
It's got an attack of 12!

14:55.940 --> 14:58.110
That's a big improvement!

14:58.110 --> 14:59.910
Okay, next...

15:00.180 --> 15:01.630
I need some armor!

15:04.320 --> 15:05.960
Thanks for your business!

15:11.590 --> 15:12.680
<b>Improved Physical Abilities Lv. 15
Exp 5
Archery Lv. 11</b>

15:13.300 --> 15:14.390
<b>Kick Lv. 12
Long-Distance Vision Lv. 8
Wind Magic Lv. 9</b>

15:15.060 --> 15:18.770
<b>Production Fingertips Lv. 17
Cooking Lv. 25
Woodworking Lv. 9</b>

15:16.720 --> 15:18.770
Cooking level 25?

15:19.960 --> 15:23.300
Oh, I've got to hurry!

15:23.910 --> 15:28.010
<i>I used a lot of my money 
to buy that armor...</i>

15:30.280 --> 15:32.630
<i>I need to earn some more cash.</i>

15:34.160 --> 15:36.410
<b>[Uncommon Healing Potion (Grape Flavor)]
Effect: Recover 18% HP</b>

15:36.640 --> 15:41.980
<i>And I'll also put in my new prototype 
grape-flavored potions to try them out, too.</i>

15:43.330 --> 15:45.790
Potion (Grape Flavor)
Rabbithorn Steak
Fried Vegetables With Meat
Pseudo Herb Tea

15:55.720 --> 15:58.470
<i>I'll start with the wolf, 
since it's closest.</i>

15:58.470 --> 16:01.980
<b>Sneak</b>

16:03.190 --> 16:04.310
Hawk Shot!

16:08.420 --> 16:10.960
It's a lot easier to 
fight with this new bow!

16:10.960 --> 16:13.450
Okay, time to get to work!

16:14.270 --> 16:16.390
Veni Ventus Volare!

16:16.390 --> 16:18.130
Wind Needle!

16:17.740 --> 16:18.330
<b>Wind Needle</b>

16:21.390 --> 16:24.530
Veni Gutadia Acrus Ratula!

16:22.330 --> 16:24.040
<b>Wind Cutter</b>

16:24.530 --> 16:26.100
Wind Cutter!

16:28.090 --> 16:29.920
<b>[Spider's Silk]
Spider silk that's so tough,
you could use it to climb out of Hell
if you had to.</b>

16:28.090 --> 16:29.920
<b>[Spider's Leg]
Useful for making the
 joints in crafted items.</b>

16:28.090 --> 16:29.920
<b>[Worm Body Fluid]
A coating that can be used
to make items long-lasting.</b>

16:28.090 --> 16:29.920
<b>[Worm Scales]
An item that is perfect
 for patching armor.</b>

16:28.090 --> 16:29.920
<b>[Wolf Pelt]
A sturdy pelt that is ideal for making capes.</b>

16:28.090 --> 16:29.920
<b>[Wolf Fangs]
A good-luck charm
that reduces the chance of
 unnecessary encounters.</b>

16:29.920 --> 16:34.290
<i>My kick and wind magic skills have 
gone up along with my archery.</i>

16:35.330 --> 16:39.940
<i>All right. I've got a lot of items 
and I'm running out of arrows.</i>

16:39.940 --> 16:41.340
<i>Time to head back.</i>

16:43.270 --> 16:44.770
<b>It's good but I could
only buy one. Add more!</b>

16:43.270 --> 16:44.770
<b>The juice was amazing!!</b>

16:45.060 --> 16:48.790
<i>But my excitement only lasted for a moment.</i>

16:48.790 --> 16:54.420
<i>Shortly after this, we were all 
brutally attacked by a new system.</i>

16:54.630 --> 16:57.730
I apologizing for using the shout function.
 Please sell me a potion!

16:57.730 --> 17:00.320
Does anybody have the medicine skill?

17:00.320 --> 17:02.380
I'll buy them for 30 gloh 
if you have spares!

17:02.380 --> 17:04.040
Please! I need potions!

17:04.040 --> 17:05.950
What's going on?

17:06.270 --> 17:09.660
You can buy all the potions you 
want from the NPCs, right?

17:10.700 --> 17:12.850
Zwei, this is Earth.

17:12.850 --> 17:14.730
Is that you, Earth?

17:15.080 --> 17:19.130
<i>I got back from hunting and the whole town's 
filled with people looking for potions.</i>

17:19.130 --> 17:20.630
<i>What happened?</i>

17:20.630 --> 17:25.270
The NPCs have started 
saying they're out of potions!

17:26.150 --> 17:28.740
That's pretty bad, though, right?

17:28.740 --> 17:32.850
<i>It is bad! For you!</i>

17:32.850 --> 17:34.960
<i>Those potion juices you sold 
at the vending machine...</i>

17:34.960 --> 17:37.300
<i>They're gonna be begging you for them!</i>

17:38.190 --> 17:39.560
It's the chef!

17:38.920 --> 17:40.290
I guess you're right!

17:38.970 --> 17:41.220
The chef who can make potions!

17:40.290 --> 17:41.520
<i>They're there already, huh?</i>

17:41.220 --> 17:43.670
I'll pay! Just give me some now!

17:41.520 --> 17:43.660
<i>I'm on my way!</i>

17:43.660 --> 17:45.830
Thanks!

17:45.830 --> 17:46.870
Please!

17:46.870 --> 17:48.460
We all need your help!

17:48.460 --> 17:50.790
You can make potions, right?

17:51.040 --> 17:53.040
Wait!

17:53.040 --> 17:54.710
I know you need potions!

17:54.710 --> 17:57.060
But there's so many people here!

17:57.060 --> 17:59.360
I'm putting a limit on how many you can buy!

17:59.360 --> 18:02.110
Potions are 40 gloh each, 
and you can only buy five!

18:04.010 --> 18:05.680
Okay!

18:06.690 --> 18:08.480
Hurry up!

18:06.690 --> 18:08.480
Dumbass!

18:10.880 --> 18:11.730
Earth.

18:12.850 --> 18:14.450
Zwei! Millie!

18:14.450 --> 18:18.360
I'll deal with the crowd control. 
You just make the potions.

18:18.360 --> 18:21.190
I'll handle the money, okay?

18:22.400 --> 18:23.750
Thanks so much.

18:24.020 --> 18:25.750
<i>I don't have a choice.</i>

18:25.750 --> 18:29.630
<i>Everybody thought medicine was a
 trash skill, so barely anybody took it.</i>

18:29.630 --> 18:32.660
<i>I don't want all the players to be 
upset because nobody has potions.</i>

18:32.670 --> 18:34.550
<b>Crafting</b>

18:32.670 --> 18:34.550
<b>Batch Crafting</b>

18:38.010 --> 18:39.430
<b>Weed</b>

18:38.010 --> 18:39.430
<b>Medicinal
Herb</b>

18:38.010 --> 18:39.430
<b>Antidote
Herb</b>

18:38.010 --> 18:39.430
<b>Wild
Herb</b>

18:39.630 --> 18:41.420
I'm out of medicinal herbs.

18:41.420 --> 18:44.450
I'm sorry! I'm out of medicinal herbs!

18:44.450 --> 18:46.920
These are the last potions 
I have for the day!

18:47.310 --> 18:49.130
Seriously? Oh, well.

18:49.130 --> 18:50.740
Make some more tomorrow, okay?

18:50.740 --> 18:51.680
Sure.

18:51.680 --> 18:53.080
Sorry, everyone!

18:53.080 --> 18:53.990
Hey!

18:56.600 --> 18:58.900
Hey, loser archer.

18:58.900 --> 19:01.530
Give me all the potions you've got.

19:01.530 --> 19:03.280
We'll make good use of them for you.

19:03.500 --> 19:05.120
Sorry.

19:05.120 --> 19:07.590
These are for the people who stood in line.

19:09.180 --> 19:10.760
You've got some nerve, don't you?

19:11.460 --> 19:13.990
Hey! Leave us alone!

19:15.370 --> 19:16.340
Zwei!

19:17.430 --> 19:21.710
I'll show you what happens 
if you don't do what I say.

19:21.710 --> 19:24.590
I'll say the exact same thing to you.

19:25.530 --> 19:28.570
You don't seem to understand the 
situation everyone's in right now.

19:33.490 --> 19:35.380
Who are you guys?

19:35.380 --> 19:37.740
You're going to take this loser's side?

19:38.100 --> 19:41.410
You shouldn't get any ideas 
about stealing them.

19:42.920 --> 19:44.750
Fine. I'll pay.

19:45.320 --> 19:49.990
What do you think will happen if we can't 
buy weapons and armor from the NPCs,

19:49.990 --> 19:52.170
like what just happened with the potions?

19:53.660 --> 19:57.000
You're going to need craftspeople!

19:57.390 --> 20:00.970
Which means you'll need to get 
along with other players!

20:01.900 --> 20:06.360
And if you make an enemy 
out of everyone here,

20:06.360 --> 20:10.090
you'll end up with nobody 
willing to sell you anything!

20:10.320 --> 20:14.180
Don't you dare lecture me!

20:14.180 --> 20:16.310
Who do you think you are, anyway?

20:18.780 --> 20:20.990
Ward...
has sent
a request...

20:19.610 --> 20:24.920
Hey, don't try to PvP him!

20:24.920 --> 20:26.620
Don't worry.

20:26.620 --> 20:30.360
I can't just let players like 
him boss everybody around!

20:30.830 --> 20:32.500
<b>Do you accept the duel?</b>

20:40.750 --> 20:43.340
<i>He thinks he's won already, I bet.</i>

20:43.340 --> 20:44.850
<i>That's fine by me.</i>

20:44.850 --> 20:48.340
<i>His arrogance gives me a chance 
to hit him in his weak spot!</i>

20:56.760 --> 20:58.960
<i>I shift to the side to dodge, and...</i>

21:03.150 --> 21:04.040
<i>There!</i>

21:05.170 --> 21:08.570
<i>Archers can't do anything but steal 
other people's points from long-range!</i>

21:08.570 --> 21:11.790
<i>But he's fighting up close?!</i>

21:27.010 --> 21:28.950
He's amazing, Millie!

21:28.950 --> 21:30.750
Get Blue Color together, now!

21:30.750 --> 21:31.720
Okay!

21:33.690 --> 21:35.530
Sorry for the trouble!

21:35.530 --> 21:39.350
I'll go get some more medicinal herbs and
 open my shop again tomorrow, okay?

21:41.490 --> 21:45.080
<i>All my hard work paid off today.</i>

21:45.740 --> 21:49.250
<i>I bet the guy with the mohawk and his buddies</i>

21:49.250 --> 21:52.850
<i>will find themselves ignored 
by all the craftspeople, now.</i>

21:53.540 --> 21:55.960
<i>And they'll end up quitting the game, too, I bet.</i>

21:55.960 --> 21:57.710
<i>Poor guys.</i>

22:03.210 --> 22:05.920
<b>From Zwei:
Earth!
Join our party!!</b>

22:05.920 --> 22:08.430
From Zwei:
Earth!
Join our party!!

22:08.430 --> 22:09.890
<b>To Be Continued</b>
